<h4>The Anee Auto agreement</h4>
<p class="au-t-ver">Version of {{ \Illuminate\Support\Carbon::parse(\App\Support\Legal::AUTO_VERSION)->format('j F Y') }}. It works together with the <a href="{{ url('/legal/eula') }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">End User License Agreement</a>, the <a href="{{ url('/legal/terms') }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Terms of Service</a> and the <a href="{{ url('/legal/privacy') }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

<h5>1. What Anee Auto does</h5>
<p>Anee Auto is a tool inside anee.io. From what you told it about your farm and from the data anee.io keeps, Anee writes a plan for the whole season, then every morning tells you and your workers the day's work, and moves the work when the weather, your crew or your reports change. You do not have to work out what to do each day: Anee tells you, and you follow. But following is always your choice.</p>

<h5>2. Anee is a guide. You stay in charge.</h5>
<p>Everything Anee Auto gives you, the protocol, the daily tasks, the timing, the products and amounts, the moves around the weather, the worker plan, the costs and the yield estimates, is guidance made automatically by software, including artificial intelligence. It is not an order and not professional advice.</p>
<ul>
<li>You can override any decision at any time. Tell Anee what you want in the season page: type it, say a day cannot be done, report what you see. She adjusts the plan to what you tell her.</li>
<li>You decide what is done on your farm, when and by whom. If a task does not fit what you see in the field, do not do it, and tell Anee.</li>
<li>Look at your field before you act, and check serious problems with a qualified person, such as your local agricultural technician or an agronomist.</li>
</ul>

<h5>3. Why Anee is still worth following</h5>
<p>Anee's plan comes from a scientific approach and deep analysis: years of weather records for your town, the forecast, the climate outlook, your soil, water and crop stage, the needs of your variety, registered products and your own reports, weighed together every day. That gives you a better chance than guessing. But no plan, and no technician, can see everything.</p>

<h5>4. What no one can foresee</h5>
<p>Farming meets things that cannot be known in advance, including:</p>
<ul>
<li>the weather on your own field (micro weather and microclimate), sudden storms, typhoons, floods, drought, heat and cold, and forecasts that change after a plan is made;</li>
<li>pests, diseases and weeds that arrive or spread unexpectedly, including ones that resist products;</li>
<li>differences in soil, water and drainage within the same lot;</li>
<li>the quality of seeds, fertilizers and chemicals, including fake, old or badly stored products;</li>
<li>how and when the work is really done, by whom, with what equipment, and in what amounts;</li>
<li>market prices, buyers, transport and the cost of inputs;</li>
<li>information you gave that is missing, outdated or wrong, and errors in outside data, maps or price records;</li>
<li>breaks in the internet, your phone, email or the app.</li>
</ul>
<p>So the plan can be incomplete, late or wrong for your field. anee.io does not promise any harvest, yield, quality, price, income or saving.</p>

<h5>5. No responsibility for what happens on the farm</h5>
<p>To the fullest extent the law allows, anee.io, its owners, staff, partners and suppliers are not responsible for any loss or damage that comes from using Anee Auto, or from following, partly following or not following its plan, tasks or answers. This includes loss of crops, yield, quality, animals, income or profit, damage to land, water, equipment or property, injury, fines, and any indirect or consequential loss. If, despite this, anee.io is found responsible, its total responsibility is limited to the credits you paid for this Anee Auto season.</p>

<h5>6. Chemicals, safety and the law</h5>
<ul>
<li>Before any fertilizer, pesticide or other chemical, read and follow its label and the law: the right product, dose, protective equipment and the waiting time before harvest. Never go above the label rate because of a task.</li>
<li>Use only registered products. Product names in Anee Auto are examples to help you find what fits, not endorsements.</li>
<li>Follow official weather warnings and your local government's instructions before any task. Keep yourself and your workers safe; do not work in a storm or flood because a task says so.</li>
</ul>

<h5>7. Your workers and your records</h5>
<ul>
<li>You are responsible for your workers: their safety, their training, their pay and how they use the app. Pay counts in Anee Auto are a help; check them before you pay.</li>
<li>The shed, costs and yield figures depend on what you record. Check them, and keep your own copies of anything important.</li>
<li>Keep your reports honest and timely: Anee can only adjust to what she is told.</li>
</ul>

<h5>8. The season, its credits and changes</h5>
<ul>
<li>Once the season starts, its answers and protocol are fixed. You steer it by telling Anee what happened, what you saw or what you want.</li>
<li>The credits for the season were taken when it was made and are not returned, whatever the season brings, as the Terms of Service describe. Questions and readings of the field come with an allowance a lot; past it, each costs the credits the app shows first.</li>
<li>You may stop following Anee Auto at any time. anee.io may improve Anee Auto during the season.</li>
</ul>

<h5>9. Your agreement</h5>
<p>By reading this to the end, ticking the box and starting the season, you confirm that you understand that Anee Auto is a guide, that you stay in charge of your farm and can override it at any time, that no one can foresee everything a season brings, and that anee.io is not responsible for what happens on your farm, as set out above. This agreement is governed by the laws of the Republic of the Philippines. If any part of it cannot be enforced, the rest still applies.</p>
<p class="au-t-end">End of the agreement.</p>
